      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{68098a4626271974ef4d2775|full_name} Just because community guidelines disallows it doesn't prevent how easily abusable these features are anyway. \n\nVrcsdk allows you to displace audio sources and materials as far as the maximum hitbox size, which, with avatar scaling, can be over 250 meters.\n\nOne can easily make an avatar that is just a 250 meter wide hitbox full of small  high pitch audio sources, use a material to hide their nameplate, and proceed to spam an instance. A single 16,000 khz squealing tone only uses less than 1kb of memory and can be looped easily. If you want to blow up peoples headphones/speakers you can do a low pass 700hz drone on loop with some mild distortion.\n\nBecause nobody knows who this person is, due to their avatar being impossible to see, and said avatar being in the good/excellent range due to having no mesh, armature, and only a handful of audio files, will likely be shown by most people on the default safety settings.\n\nYou can basically make avatars specifically designed to blow out peoples eardrums, and nobody is capable of seeing/finding them, because vrchat has no method of finding audio sources.\n\nThe existence of saftey settings isn't an excuse to like, not have the ability to not have your ears fucking destroyed on someone else's whim because they have a surface level knowledge of sound design and how the sdk functions.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
    {
