      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "This would be so helpful. This is one of the number one issues I run into when hosting meets for groups, and is one of the hardest to moderate, because once the audio playback ends, its even harder to figure out who it came from, and even then, that's only if the sound wasn't global. It's not only one of the hardest things to do to find a player responsible for an avi sound, it's also the situation where I've had the most issues of never being able to catch the person who did it, which has meant on multiple occasions, I've had to kind of awkwardly go around to everyone in the instance and be like \"Hey, as a reminder, global avi sounds or highly disruptive avi sounds aren't allowed in this group's instances\", and apologizing to everyone for not being able to resolve it in a way that is satisfactory. Right now, finding people who pull things like that a lot of the time, can feel like barely more than a witch hunt.\n\nLike if it could just be like a different color of nameplate highlight for avatar sounds, or something like that, it'd be so helpful.\n\nHonestly, extended from this, which I may make a separate feedback suggestion about this also, now that its in my head, if it's possible, if players could make instances that automatically disabled global avatar sounds, sounds that are too loud, or even just disable avi sounds, fully, it would be super helpful. Even more helpful would be is if it were that instance masters and group moderators had the options to toggle them on and off in the instance options our quick menus.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
